    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47348" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμί-φωνος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>half-pronounced</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέξις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristaenet.
					1.10
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμίφωνον, τό</span>, <i>a semi-vowel</i>, as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ρ ς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1456b27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Po.</u>
				2.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.T.
				631.16
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>half able to speak</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				6.3
			</span></i>; <i>half-vocal</i>, of certain signs of the Zodiac, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
				1.166
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				5.24
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμι-φωνία</span></b> , ἡ, <i><span class="en">
				Steph.
				<u>in Hp.</u>
				1.184D.
			</span></i></div>
